-      "body": "# Choose evidence tools\n\nOpen **Search → Evidence tools** to choose a guided Code, Documents, Evidence,\nReview or Strategies view. These are the existing workflows, not a generic tool\nrunner. The older Explore evidence drawer, command entries and deep links remain.\n\n- **Code:** symbols, textual references and selected-source outline. Written\n  references are not resolved cross-file bindings.\n- **Documents:** facts with extraction limits and original page/slide/sheet locations.\n- **Evidence:** Inspector, Check citations and Indexed changes. Preserve saved-source\n  checks, publication/baseline identity, coverage and bounded continuation.\n- **Review:** Git staged/worktree changes, bounded impact and test candidates.\n  Candidate tests are not executed tests; semantic impact is not complete.\n- **Strategies:** Library, Studio and Planner keep their source checks, manual\n  handoffs, complete exports and explicit save/import/overwrite safeguards.\n\nUse **Back to Evidence tools**, then **Continue** to return to the last guided\nview. In the same window and authority, a direct hub visit retains that view's\ninputs and complete result. Changing project/selection/trust invalidates retained\nview custody. A reload can remember the inert route, not restore read authority.\n\nThe browser hub offers guided Code, Documents, Evidence, Review and Strategies\nviews using the named sources applied in that browser session. Browser Review\nuses explicitly supplied paths or a pasted diff; it cannot observe the editor's\nGit worktree. Browser Planner supports file import and complete exports, with\nexplicit replacement confirmation. Editor-only source opening and local saves\nare not simulated. Indexed changes retain the original baseline, filters and\npublication across **Load more indexed changes** pages; keep reading while more\npages remain. A changed publication requires a new comparison.\n\nThe browser native read form remains available separately and does not adopt a\nVS Code window's scope. Choosing a hub entry only navigates; it never\ncreates/indexes/deletes, executes a query or authorizes an operation."
+      "body": "# Choose evidence tools\n\nOpen **Search → Evidence tools** to choose a guided Code, Documents, Evidence,\nReview or Strategies view. These are the existing workflows, not a generic tool\nrunner. Code, Documents, Evidence, Review and Strategies also have their own\nrail destinations. Command entries and deep links remain available.\n\n- **Code:** symbols, textual references and selected-source outline. Written\n  references are not resolved cross-file bindings.\n- **Documents:** facts with extraction limits and original page/slide/sheet locations.\n- **Evidence:** Inspector, Check citations and Indexed changes. Preserve saved-source\n  checks, publication/baseline identity, coverage and bounded continuation.\n- **Review:** Git staged/worktree changes, bounded impact and test candidates.\n  Candidate tests are not executed tests; semantic impact is not complete.\n- **Strategies:** Library, Studio and Planner keep their source checks, manual\n  handoffs, complete exports and explicit save/import/overwrite safeguards.\n\nUse **Back to Evidence tools**, then **Continue** to return to the last guided\nview. In the same window and authority, a direct hub visit retains that view's\ninputs and complete result. Changing project/selection/trust invalidates retained\nview custody. A reload can remember the inert route, not restore read authority.\n\nThe browser hub offers guided Code, Documents, Evidence, Review and Strategies\nviews using the named sources applied in that browser session. Browser Review\nuses explicitly supplied paths or a pasted diff; it cannot observe the editor's\nGit worktree. Browser Planner supports file import and complete exports, with\nexplicit replacement confirmation. Editor-only source opening and local saves\nare not simulated. Indexed changes retain the original baseline, filters and\npublication across **Load more indexed changes** pages; keep reading while more\npages remain. A changed publication requires a new comparison.\n\nThe browser native read form remains available separately and does not adopt a\nVS Code window's scope. Choosing a hub entry only navigates; it never\ncreates/indexes/deletes, executes a query or authorizes an operation."
     },
